4 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+7 & =7y-2x \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2x)+({y}^{2}-7y) & =-7 \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}y+{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}) & =-7+{1}^{2}+{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}y+{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}) & =\\frac{25}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x+1)}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{7}{2})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2} \\\\ {(x-(-1))}^{2}+{(y-\\frac{7}{2})}^{2} & ={(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(-1,\\frac{7}{2})$ and its radius is $\\frac{5}{2}.$" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432243 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432235 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432243 1069 "q-15464" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432243 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432243 1071 "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4y=12.$" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432243 1072 #uuid "1da6dc7e-65e3-5087-87df-4fd7079a93cd" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432243 1074 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+4y & =12 \\\\ {x}^{2}+({y}^{2}+4y) & =12 \\\\ {x}^{2}+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}) & =12+{2}^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2}+({y}^{2}+2\\cdot 2y+{2}^{2}) & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-0)^{2}+(y+2)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ (x-0)^{2}+(y-(-2))^{2} & ={4}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(0,-2)$ and its radius is $4.$" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432244 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432237 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432244 1069 "q-15466" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432244 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432244 1071 "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}-2x+{y}^{2}=80.$" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432244 1072 #uuid "3d51e7e2-42da-5029-94ba-a383fb96ca48" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432244 1074 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x+{y}^{2} & =80 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2x)+{y}^{2} & =80 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+{y}^{2} & =80+{1}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot x+{1}^{2})+{y}^{2} & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2} & ={9}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={9}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(1,0)$ and its radius is $9.$" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432245 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432239 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432245 1069 "q-5182" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432245 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432245 1071 "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}-12x+{y}^{2}-16y-21=0.$" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432245 1072 #uuid "81e4046d-ee12-5213-9139-6081d308b0b9" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432245 1074 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-12x+{y}^{2}-16y-21 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-12x+{y}^{2}-16y & =21 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 8y+{8}^{2}) & =21+{6}^{2}+{8}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 6x+{6}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 8y+{8}^{2}) & =121\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-6)^{2}+(y-8)^{2} & ={11}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(6,8)$ and its radius is $11.$" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432246 1068 #edb/ref 17592186432236 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432246 1069 "q-54216" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432246 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432246 1071 "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}-4x+{y}^{2}-2y=-4.$" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432246 1072 #uuid "f5b1b8a2-d088-51d1-b8fc-6a7c6d262461" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true] [17592186432246 1074 "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4x+{y}^{2}-2y & =-4 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4x)+({y}^{2}-2y) & =-4 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot y+{1}^{2}) & =-4+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot y+{1}^{2}) & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+(y-1)^{2} & ={1}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(2,1)$ and its radius is $1.$" 13194139534675 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0d6171a8-6197-560d-8edc-2b5e80c6ce81" 17592186432200 "answer-154e2e8b-b004-5fd6-a8af-0795c8960483" 17592186432201 "answer-16f43589-ba4b-5fe3-b651-27dcee807b31" 17592186432202 "answer-1bde742f-f51c-5674-bb70-2f6fd40536f4" 17592186432203 "answer-327347a6-42f8-50e6-ad5f-073e874b3720" 17592186432204 "answer-3c4c2640-0a36-56ec-af1b-fcad7796bf52" 17592186432205 "answer-4b6a21d8-b231-54b8-835d-bbc866e009e3" 17592186432206 "answer-582731db-ea16-5d66-9090-5f57ae7fd64d" 17592186432207 "answer-5a24aa32-be27-5a08-b7f2-3b7687162fe7" 17592186432208 "answer-648f4194-fec8-5e9c-87af-4fb442b8ea1e" 17592186432209 "answer-6c5d401c-bb61-5f85-be78-864bd3556574" 17592186432210 "answer-6d9f2f63-2b6c-5173-96ad-fa3cefcebd64" 17592186432211 "answer-76607376-556e-5250-8ef1-e96ff909028c" 17592186432212 "answer-7e4b8669-6cf3-5213-ae28-795579f30a2a" 17592186432213 "ans